      "showInterest": "Show interest",
      "aboutTitle": "About",
      "about1Title": "What is Model UN?",
      "about1Desc": "Model UN (MUN) is a simulation where students role-play as delegates of countries or characters. They debate real or fictional topics, follow rules of procedure, and try to pass resolutions. A Secretariat runs the conference; chairs lead each committee.",
      "about2Title": "What makes SEAMUN special?",
      "about2Desc": "Digital note passing — Send and receive notes to fellow delegates online. Personalized dashboard — Track your committee, allocations, and schedule in one place. 100% donation — All surplus goes to the Thai Red Cross Society. Student-led, non-profit, focused on global healthcare and sustainability.",
      "about3Title": "Purpose",
      "about3Desc": "100% of conference surplus is donated to the Thai Red Cross Society. We connect global policy debate with local impact.",
      "about4Title": "Collaboration",
      "about4Desc": "Delegates, chairs, and advisors work across 10 committees—resolution-writing, caucusing, and committee activities.",
      "about5Title": "Diplomacy",
      "about5Desc": "Rules of procedure, moderated debate, and formal diplomacy. We train the next generation in negotiation and public speaking.",
      "metaAudience": "Audience: Mid- and high school (grades 7–12)",
      "metaLocation": "Location: Venue TBD (Bangkok)",
      "metaFees": "Fees: 2,500 THB (school) / 3,000 THB (independent). Chair: 800 THB.",
      "metaCapacity": "Capacity: 250",
      "scheduleTitle": "Schedule",
      "scheduleDesc": "Two-day program with opening and closing ceremonies.",
